== Introduction
<introduction-14>

This class covers two of the five #strong[Wājibāt of Hajj]: the #strong[Wuqūf (وقوف)] [standing/staying] at #strong[Muzdalifah (مزدلفة)], and the beginning of the discussion on #strong[Ramī al-Jimār (رمي الجمار)] [stoning the pillars]. For Muzdalifah, the teacher discusses its status (Wājib vs Farḍ), the essential act (farḍ), the place, the time, and the ruling when it is missed. For Ramī, the class covers the dalīl for its obligation and a major #strong[uṣūl discussion] on when the #strong[actions of the Prophet ﷺ] make something obligatory --- distinguishing between obligation in #strong[practice (ʿamalī)] and obligation in #strong[creed (iʿtiqādī)], and the concept of the Prophet's #strong[khuṣūṣiyyāt (خصوصيات)] [specialties].

#horizontalrule

== Part 1 --- Status of Wuqūf at Muzdalifah
<part-1-status-of-wuquf-muzdalifah>

=== Ḥanafī position: Wājib
<hanafi-position-wajib-muzdalifah>

According to the Ḥanafī school, Wuqūf at Muzdalifah is #strong[Wājib (واجب)].

#strong[Reasoning:]

1. Its obligation is established from #strong[khabar wāḥid (خبر واحد)], which can maximally prove #strong[wujūb], not farḍiyyah.

2. The Prophet ﷺ said:

#quote(block: true)[
اَلْحَجُّ عَرَفَةُ

_"Hajj is ʿArafah."_

#strong[Ref:] Hadith --- as cited in class (confirm in hadith index).
]

If Muzdalifah were also farḍ, the Prophet ﷺ would have included it. By singling out ʿArafah, he indicated that #strong[ʿArafah alone] is the farḍ wuqūf.

3. The Prophet ﷺ #strong[sent the women and weaker members] of his family ahead from Muzdalifah before the compulsory time, allowing them to skip the wuqūf. He did #strong[not order any kaffārah] for them. A #strong[farḍ cannot be skipped] for an ʿudhr without invalidating the action --- so this proves it is only wājib.

=== Shāfiʿī position: Farḍ (Rukn)
<shafii-position-fard-muzdalifah>

According to Imam al-Shāfiʿī, Wuqūf at Muzdalifah is #strong[Farḍ].

#strong[Dalīl:]

#quote(block: true)[
فَإِذَا أَفَضْتُمْ مِنْ عَرَفَاتٍ فَاذْكُرُوا اللَّهَ عِنْدَ الْمَشْعَرِ الْحَرَامِ

_"And when you depart from ʿArafāt, then remember Allāh at al-Mashʿar al-Ḥarām."_

#strong[Ref:] Surah al-Baqarah, 2:198.
]

The āyah gives a direct #strong[command (amr)] to remember Allāh at al-Mashʿar al-Ḥarām (Muzdalifah). A command in the Qur'an refers to #strong[farḍiyyah].

=== Ḥanafī response
<hanafi-response-muzdalifah>

The Aḥnāf responded on #strong[two fronts]:

#strong[1. The meaning of "dhikr" (ذكر) is uncertain:]

The word #strong["fa-dhkurū Allāh" (فاذكروا الله)] could mean:

- #strong[The wuqūf itself] --- standing at Muzdalifah in remembrance of Allāh, OR
- #strong[The ṣalāh] --- specifically Ṣalāt al-Maghrib and Ṣalāt al-ʿIshā' combined at Muzdalifah with #strong[jamʿ ta'khīr (جمع تأخير)] [delayed combining].

Since #strong[ṣalāh is undoubtedly farḍ], the āyah could simply be commanding the prayers --- not establishing a separate farḍ of wuqūf. The #strong[uncertainty in meaning] prevents this from being a #strong[dalīl qaṭʿī].

#strong[2. The fact of ijtihād proves there is no qaṭʿī dalīl:]

The very fact that scholars had to engage in #strong[ijtihād] about whether Muzdalifah is farḍ or wājib shows that there is #strong[no definitive proof]. If there were, there would be no room for ijtihād.

#horizontalrule

== Part 2 --- The Farḍ (Essential Act) of Wuqūf at Muzdalifah
<part-2-fard-of-wuquf-muzdalifah>

=== Just being present is sufficient
<just-being-present>

The #strong[farḍ] (essential/minimum act) within the wuqūf is simply #strong[being present (الحضور)] in Muzdalifah --- in any manner:

#figure(
  align(center)[#table(
    columns: (60%, 40%),
    align: (auto, auto),
    table.header([Scenario], [Farḍ fulfilled?]),
    table.hline(),
    [Stayed properly and made duʿā'], [#strong[Yes]],
    [Merely #strong[passed through] without stopping], [#strong[Yes] --- farḍ is done],
    [Stayed for #strong[one second]], [#strong[Yes]],
    [Was present #strong[without knowing] it was Muzdalifah], [#strong[Yes] --- niyyah is not required],
    [Was present but had #strong[no intention] of wuqūf], [#strong[Yes] --- niyyah is not a shart],
  )]
  , kind: table
)

#strong[Key distinction:] The person who merely passes through fulfils the #strong[farḍ] but misses the #strong[sunnah] of proper standing with duʿā'.

=== Ṭahārah is NOT required
<tahara-not-required-muzdalifah>

#strong[Ṭahārah (طهارة)] is not a condition for the wuqūf at Muzdalifah. Ṭahārah is mandatory only for #strong[Ṭawāf], which is performed inside the Masjid. Other Hajj actions performed outside the Masjid do not require ṭahārah.

#horizontalrule

== Part 3 --- Place of Wuqūf
<part-3-place-of-wuquf>

=== Anywhere in Muzdalifah --- except Wādī Muḥassar
<anywhere-except-wadi-muhassar>

The wuqūf may be performed #strong[anywhere] within the area of Muzdalifah.

#strong[Exception:] #strong[Wādī Muḥassar (وادي محسر)] --- this valley is #strong[not] a valid place for the wuqūf. Staying there does not count.

=== Preferred location
<preferred-location-muzdalifah>

The #strong[preferred (mustaḥabb)] location is near #strong[Jabal Quzaḥ (جبل قزح)] --- the mountain near which the #strong[Imam] and #strong[Amīr of Hajj] stand. This is the same place where the Prophet ﷺ made his wuqūf. Being close to it means being:

- Closer to the #strong[Imam].
- Closer to the #strong[place of the Prophet ﷺ].

However, it is #strong[not permissible] to rush, push, or cause harm to others in trying to reach this spot.

#horizontalrule

== Part 4 --- Time of Wuqūf at Muzdalifah
<part-4-time-of-wuquf-muzdalifah>

=== The compulsory time: Between Ṣubḥ Ṣādiq and sunrise
<compulsory-time-muzdalifah>

#figure(
  align(center)[#table(
    columns: (50%, 50%),
    align: (auto, auto),
    table.header([Period], [Status]),
    table.hline(),
    [#strong[Night] (after arriving from ʿArafah, 9th Dhū al-Ḥijjah)], [#strong[Sunnah] --- spending the night is recommended, not wājib],
    [#strong[From Ṭulūʿ al-Fajr (صبح صادق) to Ṭulūʿ al-Shams (طلوع الشمس)]], [#strong[Wājib] --- this is the compulsory period for the wuqūf],
  )]
  , kind: table
)

=== Practical sequence
<practical-sequence-muzdalifah>

1. #strong[After ʿArafah] (evening of 9th Dhū al-Ḥijjah): pilgrims travel to Muzdalifah.
2. #strong[At Muzdalifah:] Ṣalāt al-Maghrib and Ṣalāt al-ʿIshā' are performed together (#strong[jamʿ ta'khīr] --- Maghrib delayed to ʿIshā' time).
3. #strong[Night:] Rest and sleep --- this is sunnah, not wājib.
4. #strong[Fajr prayer:] Should be performed #strong[as early as possible] --- in the #strong[dark part] of Fajr time (not waiting for brightness as is normally preferred in the Ḥanafī school).
5. #strong[After Fajr:] Stand (#strong[wuqūf]) facing the Qiblah, making duʿā' and dhikr, until proper daylight appears.
6. #strong[Before sunrise:] Depart for Minā.

=== Why pray Fajr early on this day?
<why-pray-fajr-early>

Normally in the Ḥanafī school, Fajr is preferred in the #strong[isfār (إسفار)] [bright period]. But on the morning of the 10th Dhū al-Ḥijjah at Muzdalifah, Fajr should be prayed #strong[early in the dark (ghalas / غلس)] --- so the pilgrim has #strong[more time] for the wuqūf and duʿā' before departing.

=== Ruling for departing early
<ruling-for-departing-early>

#figure(
  align(center)[#table(
    columns: (50%, 50%),
    align: (auto, auto),
    table.header([Scenario], [Ruling]),
    table.hline(),
    [Departed #strong[after Fajr prayer] but #strong[before standing for wuqūf]], [Farḍ of presence is done; missed the sunnah of standing --- #strong[no penalty], but against the sunnah],
    [Departed #strong[before Fajr time] entirely (left in the night)], [#strong[Wājib missed] --- if without ʿudhr, #strong[dam] is required],
  )]
  , kind: table
)

=== Imam al-Shāfiʿī's extended compulsory time
<shafii-extended-time>

Imam al-Shāfiʿī held that the compulsory time begins from the #strong[second half of the night] (after midnight of the 9th/10th Dhū al-Ḥijjah) --- not from Fajr. This extends the compulsory window.

#horizontalrule

== Part 5 --- Ruling When Wuqūf at Muzdalifah is Missed
<part-5-missed-wuquf-muzdalifah>

=== Missed with ʿudhr: No penalty
<missed-with-udhr>

The Prophet ﷺ sent the #strong[women, elderly, and weaker members] of his family ahead from Muzdalifah during the night --- before the compulsory time. He did #strong[not order any penalty] for them. This establishes:

- Weaker pilgrims, women, children, and the elderly may #strong[depart at night] before Fajr.
- The wājib is #strong[missed for ʿudhr] (crowd, physical weakness) $arrow$ #strong[no dam].

=== Missed without ʿudhr: Dam is required
<missed-without-udhr>

If a healthy, capable person leaves Muzdalifah before the compulsory time (Fajr to sunrise) #strong[without a valid excuse]:

- #strong[Dam (دم)] --- slaughter of a goat in the Ḥaram.

#horizontalrule

== Part 6 --- Ramī al-Jimār: Introduction and Dalīl
<part-6-rami-introduction>

=== Status: Wājib --- by Ijmāʿ
<rami-status-wajib>

#strong[Ramī al-Jimār (رمي الجمار)] [stoning the pillars] is #strong[wājib] and agreed upon by #strong[all schools of thought] as a compulsory act of Hajj.

=== Dalīl
<rami-dalil>

1. #strong[Ijmāʿ (إجماع):] The entire Ummah agrees on its obligation.
2. #strong[The Prophet's statement:] He ordered the performance of Ramī.
3. #strong[The Prophet's practice (fiʿl / فعل):] He performed Ramī in his Hajj.
4. #strong[His general instruction:]

#quote(block: true)[
خُذُوا عَنِّي مَنَاسِكَكُمْ

_"Learn your rites (of Hajj) from me."_

#strong[Ref:] Hadith --- as cited in class (confirm in hadith index).
]

#horizontalrule

== Part 7 --- Major Uṣūl: When Does the Prophet's Action (Fiʿl) Establish Wujūb?
<part-7-usul-prophets-action>

The teacher explained a critical #strong[uṣūl principle] regarding when the actions of the Prophet ﷺ create obligation for the Ummah.

=== Three conditions for the Prophet's action to establish wujūb
<three-conditions-prophets-action>

#figure(
  align(center)[#table(
    columns: (5%, 30%, 65%),
    align: (center, auto, auto),
    table.header([*\#*], [Condition], [Explanation]),
    table.hline(),
    [1], [#strong[Done with consistency (مواظبة)]], [He performed it regularly, not just once or occasionally],
    [2], [#strong[Done as ʿibādah (عبادة), not personal need]], [It was performed as worship, not to fulfil a personal or natural need],
    [3], [#strong[Not his khuṣūṣiyyah (خصوصية)]], [It was not something exclusive to him --- must be applicable to the Ummah generally],
  )]
  , kind: table
)

=== The distinction: ʿAmalī vs Iʿtiqādī wujūb
<amali-vs-itiqadi-wujub>

#figure(
  align(center)[#table(
    columns: (35%, 65%),
    align: (auto, auto),
    table.header([Type], [Meaning]),
    table.hline(),
    [#strong[Wājib ʿAmalī (واجب عملي)]], [The Ummah #strong[must perform] the action --- obligatory to practise upon it],
    [#strong[Wājib Iʿtiqādī (واجب اعتقادي)]], [It is #strong[declared wājib in one's belief] --- one must hold it to be wājib as a matter of conviction],
  )]
  , kind: table
)

#strong[When the Prophet's action (with the three conditions) is the sole evidence:]

- It establishes #strong[wājib ʿamalī] --- we must follow it in practice.
- It does #strong[NOT] establish #strong[wājib iʿtiqādī] --- we cannot declare it wājib as a matter of creed.

#strong[Why?] Because there is always a #strong[possibility] that the action was the Prophet's #strong[khuṣūṣiyyah] (specialty). We cannot be certain it applies to the Ummah. Therefore:

- #strong[Practice:] We must follow it (out of caution --- if it is wājib and we do it, we fulfil the obligation; if it turns out to be optional and we do it, there is no harm).
- #strong[Creed:] We cannot declare it definitively wājib (because of the possibility of khuṣūṣiyyah).

=== In the case of Ramī al-Jimār
<rami-beyond-fiil>

For Ramī, the matter is #strong[beyond just the Prophet's action] --- there is also his #strong[explicit verbal order] and #strong[Ijmāʿ]. Therefore, Ramī is established as wājib both #strong[ʿamalī and iʿtiqādī].

=== Examples of Khuṣūṣiyyāt (the Prophet's specialties)
<examples-of-khususiyyat>

#figure(
  align(center)[#table(
    columns: (25%, 25%, 50%),
    align: (auto, auto, auto),
    table.header([Action], [Status], [Why it is khuṣūṣiyyah]),
    table.hline(),
    [#strong[Tahajjud (تهجد)]], [Was #strong[farḍ upon the Prophet ﷺ] only], [He performed it with consistency as ʿibādah, but it was his specialty --- not farḍ on the Ummah],
    [#strong[Marrying more than four wives]], [His #strong[exclusive permission]], [The general Qur'anic limit for the Ummah is #strong[four]; no one may follow him in this, not even as sunnah],
  )]
  , kind: table
)

#strong[Key point:] When an action is declared the Prophet's khuṣūṣiyyah, it means #strong[no one else may perform it] --- not as wājib, not as sunnah, not even as mubāḥ. Otherwise, the designation of "khuṣūṣiyyah" would lose its meaning.

#horizontalrule

